# SHA-512 and SHA-384 (FIPS 180-4) and HMAC over both (RFC 2104), in Rae. SHA-384 is SHA-512 with
# other starting values, cut to 48 bytes: ECDSA on P-384 signs a SHA-384 hash (crypto/P384, the
# certificates of Apple's own CAs in an App Store chain). The 64-bit words are UInt64, whose
# arithmetic wraps as the standard's does.

# The round constants: the first 64 bits of the fractional parts of the cube roots of the first
# 80 primes
